checks_run.procedure:
Probes on with-stack.sh, in en and ar, in both locale settings:
- (A) a read-only AUD pass over 19 P6 screens, plus every P6 mutation via the API;
- (B) reflow at 360 px and 390 px and with 200 % text, for dev.admin and dev.lead;
- (C) a 400 validation error shown in the selected language;
- (D) REQ-S17-001 row counts on screen;
- (E) REQ-S02-006: clear all browser storage;
- XSS payloads on the evidence, register and search screens;
- axe, reflow and AUD on the two detail screens no suite opens;
- the breadcrumb Tab order;
- the F-DG6-261 probe;
- p3-ui-completion and the deliverable-count probe.

checks_run.actual:
913 dotted codes were found; the 271 unmatched hits are mostly audit actions, permissions and SQL columns from the tuple and ternary patterns. 48 come from the problem-bearing patterns. Most are covered, by namespace:
- translated in their own namespace: assistant.refused.*, charter.*, import.row.*, initiative.*, schedule.unknown;
- field-error codes with the localized generic fallback problems.validation__invalid: validation.credential_refs, commit_on_behalf_of and unknown_version;
- the assistant provider codes, shown inside a localized sentence (assistant.reply.unavailable);
- shown as identifiers in admin tables or studio check results by design (smtp.*, compatibility.*, preview.*).
None of these is an English leak. The HTTP problem codes are covered, as problems-all.test.ts claims. The gap is two operational-exception codes: kpi.stale, raised by the worker as DATA_STALE_ERROR_CODE, and operations.heartbeat_missed, raised by the API watch. Neither has a catalogue text, so FE-Z2's ExceptionErrorText shows the raw code as 'Last error' in both languages. Live: 'shown="operations.heartbeat_missed" catalogueText=false'. The connector codes are localized ('لم يستجب نظام المصدر.'). I raise this as F-DG6-320: Low, cosmetic, admin screen only, not blocking.

All four P6 drills pass in run 1, run 2 and tests/qa:
- channel send: 13.9-14.7 s;
- import commit: 4.9-6.1 s;
- reindex: 9.3 s;
- connector run: about 122 s.
The worker restart, export-job kill and Day-90 tests pass too. Outbound write-once passes 3 of 3 in each run. O-1 passes in both runs, as does the 'at most jobConcurrency run at once' test. In the job logs, run 1 and run 2 each have 305 outcomes on the backlog rules: 245 succeeded, each with a distinct executionId, and 60 marked duplicate. 0 executionIds succeeded twice. packages/config/src/load.ts sets WORKER_JOB_BATCH_SIZE default 8 and WORKER_JOB_CONCURRENCY default 4.

Driver exit 0. Dataset: 50 transformations, 1000 initiatives, 10000 KPI actuals, 100000 audit events and 120 users, 154 MB, generated in 28 s. The UUID check found 120 non-RFC values out of 770559, the migration-seeded rows found in round 3. Steady-state p95 per class:
- read 18.1 ms (n 7542);
- update 29.1 ms (n 2079);
- search 17.6 ms;
- dashboard 40.2 ms (n 3766);
- export start 38.2 ms.
There were 0 errors, 0 conflicts, 0 rate-limit refusals and 0 error-level log lines. No class missed its target. getWorkstreamDashboard is 'not measured' because the profile has no workstream, a residual the register discloses. export-proof part A: 16 exports, each started with 202 (p95 98 ms); each reached 100 % (completion p95 2.12 s); the other user and AUD got 404 on both the job and the download. Part B: 50 transformations at once, start p95 663 ms, completion p95 4.42 s. 428 export jobs succeeded, with at most 1 assembly attempt and 0 pending. export-proof exits 1 only on 'LOAD-T20 FAIL: no sameScopeOther user for this transformation', the dataset gap disclosed in REQ-S20-030's note; it is not a latency or access failure.

All 48 rows are IMPLEMENTED, and 13 changed since round 3 (AN-Z2). Deferrals re-run here and passed:
- REQ-S12-019: the A17 failing connector, in both root runs, en and ar;
- REQ-S15-014: the term scan, in both root runs;
- REQ-S17-007: A12-5 (assistant);
- REQ-S16-027: 932 operations;
- REQ-S16-029: log-redaction and the log-scan self-test;
- REQ-S10-002 and REQ-S10-004: A12 plus BE-Z4's registers test;
- REQ-S20-001, -012, -017 and -022: QA-R4-VERIF.
The disclosed partials are unchanged from round 3 and still acceptable:
